WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Lighting and visibility. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Map visible zones and constraints

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Lighting design must account for what the driver can see and what others can see. A styling sketch alone cannot establish compliance.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Draw the lamp, target directions and nearby body occlusion; identify the test rule and jurisdiction separately.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Coverage diagram

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: A view supports interpretation; it cannot prove hidden structure or compliance alone.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Map visible zones and constraints
